I applied two of the four findings and rejected two, both with reasons. Both fixes are in /Users/qc25212/Downloads/Misc/Games and apps/Cath Simulator/src/ui/sections/HaemoLab.tsx.

Applied:
- Finding 2 (heading capitals): the recorded-pressures heading now lowercases only the first letter of the set title, so it reads 'Recorded pressures, before PCI (mmHg)' and 'after PCI'. There is no test for this: the default HaemoLab render has no measurement sets, so the heading never appears in it.
- Finding 3 (array events crash): launchStudy() now reads p.events as unknown. It splits a string on commas, takes an array as it is, and treats any other type as no events. Each name is converted with String() and trimmed before it is checked against LAB_EVENTS, so an array no longer throws inside the store subscriber. I exported launchStudy (a named export alongside the default component) so it can be tested.

New test: a 'haemodynamics lab launch' block in /Users/qc25212/Downloads/Misc/Games and apps/Cath Simulator/src/ui/haemo/panels.test.ts. It checks that:
- a string with one valid and one invalid name keeps only 'hypotension';
- an array does not throw and gives ['hypotension'];
- a number gives [];
- an unknown scenario returns null.

Out of scope (finding 1): event gates for four tips in src/content/manual/cath-handbook/04-cardiac-catheterisation.ts and 06-additional-procedures.ts; the rejected list above has the details. No other files outside the package were touched.
